The system should communicate this fantasy:

The player is not collecting dead people's souls.

The player is inheriting what the world remembers about them.

Cards represent those inheritances.

Echoes represent the player's own accumulated journey.

Memories reveal the people behind the cards.

Death Echoes preserve the player's own last moments.

The mechanics should reinforce this narrative rather than simply rename Souls mechanics.

